 and remember he  wasn't  arguably too much to blame for pedro  either  so it's interesting finding out about  what kind of guy this antagonist is  he was down to team up with marco he's  obviously punishing carrick for  trespassing in their territory because  he's a pirate  but he doesn't mercilessly kill her  which would obviously be the smart thing  to do  if their fight was actually a close call  as he said he even warns her that if she  doesn't want to mourn  any more of her friends she should hop  back to the woods and chew on some grass  of course he seems like a huge jerk and  i'm sure we all hate seeing anyone hurt  the incredibly cute karachon  but honestly you can expect a pirate to  do much worse than perospero did here  especially to someone who wants revenge  against them at the end of the day  i find what he didn't do more  interesting than what he did do  he's going to be fascinating to watch in  this arc he strolls off and says he's  still against allying with the beast  pirates  but we must teach these upstarts what it  means to be an emperor  again nothing personal there just  carrying out pirate business  and he still emphasizes that he's  against allying with the beast pirates  even after everything big mom said to  him could he  actually help marco after all all i know  is that my  eyes are gonna be glued to peril sparrow  during this arc  and i can't wait to see what he ends up  doing we jump to chopper working on the  cure while everyone struggles to  preserve themselves the flames from  marco help while people have stamina but  people are fast approaching their limit  and they'll quickly  regress to ice demons if something  doesn't change quick  another sense of urgency being thrown  into this conflict for good measure  if this happens the ice demons will  rampage and eventually die from  exhaustion  but not before spreading the ice demon  illness to more people  up who is still standing as subordinates  look to him for guidance  they wonder why queen would expose them  to this while puss has quit your  whimpering  since queen won't be moved by it  although i'm not a huge fan of apu  never was you gotta give him his props  here he's still on his feet and he's  calm cool and collected at the same time  refusing to whine because it won't do  him any good and he knows it  the wall keeping them from chopper is  made up of a canadian rapper and a  yakuza flower  if drake were to switch sides again that  would be truly terrible for us  but he's been reliable so far and  hyogoro is back to his prime judging  from outward appearances  they straight up say that the yakuza  boss is too strong and they can't get  close to chopper who they hilariously  keep calling a tanuki  or japanese raccoon dog so how did  hyogoro  go from being a shriveled up old geezer  to his prime physique  well he explains that being exposed to  the ice demon virus  may have brought him close to death but  it also seems to have drawn out his  dormant strength  it's one of those classic shonen  situations where at the cost of  exchanging your remaining  life force you can gain exceptional  power for a period of time  and hyogoro decides to use this power to  cut down the enemy's main forces  while bravely fighting off the ice demon  virus as best as he can  unfortunately though the ice is  spreading fast  i really like the fact that the  so-called flower got to bloom one more  time  and go out in such a powerful way at the  peak of his glory it reminds me of rock  lee saying the lotus of the hidden leaf  village blooms twice  and i love how oda handled this flower  as well  and hyogoro is just such an honorable  guy  that you can't help but respect him he  eventually tells his men that they're  gonna need to end his life without  hesitation  so he doesn't end up indiscriminately  killing everyone in the hall  before he has to go though hyogoro uses  one sword flower style against the enemy  forces  they comment that that style is obsolete 